From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: liuqin: describe the asymmetric CPU capacities

Without capacity-dmips-mhz the scheduler treats all eight CPUs as equally
capable. On Liuqin, a user-manager reload takes about 3.1 seconds on an
A510 but 0.8 seconds on an A710; leaving startup on a little CPU causes
large variations in Plasma startup time.

Use the per-MHz capacities published for this board in Xiaomi's Cape
device tree. arch_topology combines these with the discovered maximum
frequencies to produce capacities of 277, 832 and 1024 on this tablet.
Keep the frequency policies and task affinities under scheduler control.

Source: https://github.com/MiCode/kernel_devicetree/blob/1c507816ba8aa6117dcec41f577ef7a66d2091f7/qcom/cape.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -435,6 +435,39 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/* OEM Cape capacities; normalized with each cluster's maximum frequency. */
+&cpu0 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+};
+
+&cpu4 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+};
+
+&cpu5 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+};
+
+&cpu6 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+};
+
+&cpu7 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2386>;
+};
+
 &iris {
 	status = "okay";
 };
